roduced. Because the injection only removes flux, this equals max|injected - original| * 1e6.","limitations":["The requested depth parameterises rp = sqrt(depth * 1e-6); limb darkening makes the central flux decrement larger than that value.","Injection is applied to the stored processed flux, while the Phase 5 builder injected into detrended flux. The formula is identical but the displayed baseline is not detrended.","The processed CSVs carry no quality column, so no quality-bit mask can be applied here; non-finite values are dropped instead.","Measured depth is limited by cadence: with 29.4-minute Kepler sampling the transit centre may fall between exposures, so the measured value is a lower bound on the true injected decrement."]},"scientific_notice":"The injected transit is simulated and overlaid on real observations. It is not a detection, it does not reproduce the saved Phase 5 experiment, and no model is trained or evaluated by this view."}